 But a story is set there. It's one of my favourites actually; my personal favorite Storyteller character from that book takes a trip to Dubai, and hijinks ensue. My Dubai is weird. This is an understatement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:50:15-08:00","id":386299,"title":"","content":"That Changeling 2e is finally getting started fills me with joy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:06:05-08:00","id":386318,"title":"","content":"I like a lot of this. The only thing that concerns me is the Mortal Template section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortal splat section. There\u2019s been a lot of discussion here. But, essentially this is \u201cpotential targets\u201d. It\u2019s those who have had a brush, who are likely to become abductees. People who, if they play into a story the right way, can be kinda awesome and beyond the normal. </div> </div> </div>Mostly because the new mortal splats coming out tend to have powers and supernatural things that set them apart; are Changelings people who used to have these things in their normal life? Will they already be interacting with Changelings and that's why they are at a higher chance of being abducted? I feel like Ensorcelling would be a better fit for a Mortal splat, especially if you could get <i>accidentally Ensorcelled</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm worrying for nothing and it'll be awesome. But.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T07:24:02-08:00","id":386336,"title":"","content":"C'est super-chouette! Hedgespinning in the core book is awesome. I'm very curious as to how the new pledge and oneiromancy rules will look. Also, room for 100 kiths? Wow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:52:39-08:00","id":386539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386318#post386318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because the new mortal splats coming out tend to have powers and supernatural things that set them apart; are Changelings people who used to have these things in their normal life? Will they already be interacting with Changelings and that's why they are at a higher chance of being abducted? I feel like Ensorcelling would be a better fit for a Mortal splat, especially if you could get <i>accidentally Ensorcelled</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with whole heart. But Ensorcelled can also easily have higher rate of get kidnapped. with all the Faerie left-over magic on them, and still not having Wyrd to protect from Fae. Like Cinderella or Snow White - they get the little magical power <b>before</b> they interacted with Fae. And because of this, Huntsman stalked Snow White...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-31-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:56:45-08:00","id":386542,"title":"","content":"What was wrong with the old pledge system? I loved to exploit its possibilities, specially when dealing with mortals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T13:20:06-08:00","id":386629,"title":"","content":"Actually wondering about something that I hope David can answer. The approved outline has the same pointers for how to write the kith and their blessings as the draft, but the guidelines on Seeming mechanical benefits from the original are missing. Fluff I am greatly anticipating aside, is the plan still to have each Seeming add +1 to a Resistance attribute and protect the changeling from Expectional Successes of rolls with one of the six Power/Finesse attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T13:45:46-08:00","id":386657,"title":"","content":"The outline looks great. I'm excited to see how it all comes together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:20:41-08:00","id":386668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386318#post386318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like a lot of this. The only thing that concerns me is the Mortal Template section.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly because the new mortal splats coming out tend to have powers and supernatural things that set them apart; are Changelings people who used to have these things in their normal life? Will they already be interacting with Changelings and that's why they are at a higher chance of being abducted? I feel like Ensorcelling would be a better fit for a Mortal splat, especially if you could get <i>accidentally Ensorcelled</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm worrying for nothing and it'll be awesome. But.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm also a bit concerned about it. Hopefully Wyrdhamster is correct in that the Fae-Touched and Enchanted/Ensorcelled are more likely to be kidnapped. Although I kinda want Fae-Touched to get the Wolf-Blooded treatment so that they are interesting to play alongside Changelings and not just damsels/(insert male equivalent for Damsels) in distress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T17:22:53-08:00","id":386867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386542#post386542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was wrong with the old pledge system? I loved to exploit its possibilities, specially when dealing with mortals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Too fucking complicated and long. While I liked the concept, I died inside everytime someone mentioned wanting to take a pledge. Also, too many words, yet not clear enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T18:15:55-08:00","id":386886,"title":"","content":"The original Pledge system also suffered a bit by being a bit too antagonistic between the ST and the players. The system was easy to game, making breaking a pledge something that ST had to force on players to have them come up.<br /> <br /> It's similar to the problem with the cWOD Flaws vs. the nWOD Flaws/Conditions. The cWOD Flaws reward players to taking a lot of them for a lot of gain, and then doing as much as possible to make sure the downsides never bite them in the ass; so STs have to enforce them to make them matter. The nWOD Flaws/Conditions systems reward players when it actually negatively impacts them.<br /> <br /> The Pledge system had the same problem. Up-front rewards for the risk of negative consequences, but no reward for the consequences coming about; so the players are discouraged from wanting their pledges being put up for stakes; but the ST feels the need to put them at risk to make the rewards count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T18:55:50-08:00","id":386931,"title":"","content":"Re: The issue with Pledges. As one of my friends puts it, &quot;There is no reason any Changeling should be poor.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T19:57:33-08:00","id":386945,"title":"","content":"are contract going to get a power up?<br /> i had a reality shock when i started to play changeling after having played vampire and mage because, for example, while i could rule in social interactions with dominate, majesty and mind arcanum, vainglory felt like just a few bonus and tricks, nothing to big","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T20:00:49-08:00","id":386948,"title":"","content":"Changeling was more a game of stacking the deck than flipping the table, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T23:31:50-08:00","id":387120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386945#post386945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are contract going to get a power up?<br /> i had a reality shock when i started to play changeling after having played vampire and mage because, for example, while i could rule in social interactions with dominate, majesty and mind arcanum, vainglory felt like just a few bonus and tricks, nothing to big</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be some shift there. But, that's not the place you're going to see the biggest change in basic edges. Changelings will be a little different on a template level. <br /> <br /> They will be able to flip the proverbial table. But, in that case, it's going to be a question of &quot;should they?&quot; Because, you know, consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:02:48-08:00","id":387131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386285#post386285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a HUGE treatment or anything. But a story is set there. It's one of my favourites actually; my personal favorite Storyteller character from that book takes a trip to Dubai, and hijinks ensue. My Dubai is weird. This is an understatement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having lived in Abu Dhabi for the last 3 years, I feel fairly confident in saying that Duabi is always weird, no matter what the incarnation, and that it always gets understated. Anyhow, even having just a story is cool and Vampire is definitely a good one to start with. I've got a book in which I'm storing different ideas for UAE in general. Maybe I'll actually get them written up and online some day. <br /> <br /> In 1e, I recall that the seasonal courts were specifically picked by Changelings since they were tied to this reality and confused the True Fae. Is there going to be something similar in the 2e court building system? I've tossed around numerous ideas for Courts in Abu Dhabi since the seasons here, at least as my Canadian ass is concerned, are practically non-existent here. Some of these include moon phases (since there are fewer werewolves and the moon ties them thematically to Islam), locations of the sun in the sky (since its omnipresent), or the Call to Prayer times (since each has religious symbolisms and are also omnipresent), but I've also tossed around using the ideas of continental courts in Duabi since there are more ethnicities in the city than you can shake a stick at. Would any of those ideas be thematically workable do you think? I like the adaptive parallel to Mystery Cult Initiation. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:17:40-08:00","id":387141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387131#post387131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having lived in Abu Dhabi for the last 3 years, I feel fairly confident in saying that Duabi is always weird, no matter what the incarnation, and that it always gets understated. Anyhow, even having just a story is cool and Vampire is definitely a good one to start with. I've got a book in which I'm storing different ideas for UAE in general. Maybe I'll actually get them written up and online some day.<br /> <br /> In 1e, I recall that the seasonal courts were specifically picked by Changelings since they were tied to this reality and confused the True Fae. Is there going to be something similar in the 2e court building system? I've tossed around numerous ideas for Courts in Abu Dhabi since the seasons here, at least as my Canadian ass is concerned, are practically non-existent here. Some of these include moon phases (since there are fewer werewolves and the moon ties them thematically to Islam), locations of the sun in the sky (since its omnipresent), or the Call to Prayer times (since each has religious symbolisms and are also omnipresent), but I've also tossed around using the ideas of continental courts in Duabi since there are more ethnicities in the city than you can shake a stick at. Would any of those ideas be thematically workable do you think? I like the adaptive parallel to Mystery Cult Initiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Courts in 2e are forged on stories. So, you find a story, and you center your institutions and infrastructure on that story. <br /> <br /> Essentially, what Courts do is let the Court members choose the rules of engagement. The Fae (and by extension, the Huntsmen) have to play by Arcadian rules. Courts basically make those rules, in flesh space. So, when the Huntsmen are out of the Hedge, they have to abide by those rules. That's why Courts exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:23:40-08:00","id":387144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387141#post387141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Courts in 2e are forged on stories. So, you find a story, and you center your institutions and infrastructure on that story.<br /> <br /> Essentially, what Courts do is let the Court members choose the rules of engagement. The Fae (and by extension, the Huntsmen) have to play by Arcadian rules. Courts basically make those rules, in flesh space. So, when the Huntsmen are out of the Hedge, they have to abide by those rules. That's why Courts exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>How this is tied to classical Seasonal Courts? Becuase I do not see A Story on first look on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:28:36-08:00","id":387147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387144#post387144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How this is tied to classical Seasonal Courts? Becuase I do not see A Story on first look on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have an emotional aim, a set of motifs, and a preferred framework of operation, to say nothing of how Fatebound Merits include roles that differ slightly by Court. If you can't figure out a story from that then you're not trying.<br /> <br /> Courts narrow the casting calls for incoming monsters and give you a symbolset equipped to deal with the ones that make the cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:46:43-08:00","id":387150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Seeming One: This is what it looks like as a Beast. Raw<br /> . Scary. It\u2019s got fangs! You should be afraid, I promise.<br /> \u2022 Seeming Two: This is what it looks like as a Fairest. Aww. How pretty. It\u2019s got fangs! You should be turned on, I promise.<br /> \u2022 Seeming Three: This is what it looks like as a Wizened. Aww. How smart. It\u2019s got fangs! You should be asking where it got those fangs, I promise. </div> </div> </div>My favorite bit.<br /> <br /> Re: Pledges: more than giving players reasons to break their pledges I'd like to see reasons for them to trick mortals into breaking those pledges... probably with a nice Clarity roll to accompany it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T00:50:50-08:00","id":387151,"title":"","content":"Six minutes after a spoiler and wyrdhamster is on the ball complaining about how he's not being spoonfed with more details. This is why we can't have nice things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T01:09:19-08:00","id":387156,"title":"","content":"Will Budapest and Capetown have new Courts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T01:22:41-08:00","id":387161,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not intending to use the seasonal ones for Hungary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T02:32:21-08:00","id":387179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387144#post387144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How this is tied to classical Seasonal Courts? Becuase I do not see A Story on first look on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know. It's not written yet. One of the authors will be doing seasonal courts. I leave it in their capable hands to figure out how that works. <br /> <br /> Budapest, Capetown, Tokyo, and (probably Toronto?) will have new courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T02:46:37-08:00","id":387182,"title":"","content":"Still, are Seasonal Courts majority, or even just popular theme in Europe and Americas, or each Freehold have they own? I understand that 2ed corebook will show as much diffrent examples in settings to point what can be made with games framework - for the Rule of Cool - but I think still typical answer is &quot;if you do not have strong local mythical Story to use, get the Seasons&quot;, yes?<br /> <br /> Like I run <b>Mage</b> game in London - it want be sensation that local Lost NPC are still clinging to the &quot;old ways&quot; of Seasons? How about Americas - if Seasonal Courts are still a thing there? I run a <b>Changeling</b> 1ed game centered in New England were new Freehold is build in small town - I assumed that Native Americans changelings have they own Courts there, but were wiped out by True Fae. Then white colonists come with they own Seasonal Courts - and next Freehold were wiped out. In 2ed, is it still a thing, or rather colonists would make they own Courts? And modern PCs are open for they own Court system to create?<br /> <br /> Basiclly, question is - how much &quot;canon will be Seasonal Courts now, when new will spring around the globe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T03:01:06-08:00","id":387184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387179#post387179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't know. It's not written yet. One of the authors will be doing seasonal courts. I leave it in their capable hands to figure out how that works.<br /> <br /> Budapest, Capetown, Tokyo, and (probably Toronto?) will have new courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>so I assume that the Directional Courts are limited to China and the mainland with Japan having its own Courts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T04:59:05-08:00","id":387220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387182#post387182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, are Seasonal Courts majority, or even just popular theme in Europe and Americas, or each Freehold have they own? I understand that 2ed corebook will show as much diffrent examples in settings to point what can be made with games framework - for the Rule of Cool - but I think still typical answer is &quot;if you do not have strong local mythical Story to use, get the Seasons&quot;, yes?<br /> <br /> Like I run <b>Mage</b> game in London - it want be sensation that local Lost NPC are still clinging to the &quot;old ways&quot; of Seasons? How about Americas - if Seasonal Courts are still a thing there? I run a <b>Changeling</b> 1ed game centered in New England were new Freehold is build in small town - I assumed that Native Americans changelings have they own Courts there, but were wiped out by True Fae. Then white colonists come with they own Seasonal Courts - and next Freehold were wiped out. In 2ed, is it still a thing, or rather colonists would make they own Courts? And modern PCs are open for they own Court system to create?<br /> <br /> Basiclly, question is - how much &quot;canon will be Seasonal Courts now, when new will spring around the globe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has their own. I'm only featuring seasonal courts as a way to demonstrate the ability to do something 1e. There's no &quot;default&quot;. If you want to make your Storyteller characters cling to it like it's an old way, that's all well and good. We're not presenting that as a default in the book. Consider the &quot;Prince, Primogen, Prisci, Sheriff&quot; style model in Vampire. Vampire 2e did not present that as a default. That's what we're doing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T04:59:58-08:00","id":387223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387184#post387184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so I assume that the Directional Courts are limited to China and the mainland with Japan having its own Courts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really addressing the former. Not REALLY addressing the latter. I might mention Kyoto's Court, because I have an idea for it. But the sample given of Tokyo is specifically, and just, Tokyo. It is its own city, and isn't to be taken as a default for Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T05:13:01-08:00","id":387228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387223#post387223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really addressing the former. Not REALLY addressing the latter. I might mention Kyoto's Court, because I have an idea for it. But the sample given of Tokyo is specifically, and just, Tokyo. It is its own city, and isn't to be taken as a default for Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say that making the courts into local groups (around 2nd Tier, as much as that terminology is valid) makes a lot of sense- and is actually really interesting. It makes it so not only the Fae and the Huntsmen need to follow the Court's rules, but any lost changeling (pun not intended) who drops into the Court's territory. He should learn the rules quickly if he wish to enjoy that Court's protection, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T06:57:40-08:00","id":387336,"title":"","content":"I just woke up and haven't had coffee yet, but I keep imagining a Court system structured around corporate branding. The Court of Unilever. The Court of Sony. The Court of ThyssenKrupp. The Court of Last Dynasty International.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T07:54:23-08:00","id":387381,"title":"","content":"I like the custom court idea. The Courts of Manhattan are Bull and Bear, changing power with the economy. The courts of Washington DC are an alphabet soup of changeling &quot;agencies&quot; that have a complicated bureaucratic structure adjusting their authority; or maybe there is the court of the Elephant and the court of the Donkey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:46:23-08:00","id":387534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387141#post387141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Courts in 2e are forged on stories. So, you find a story, and you center your institutions and infrastructure on that story.<br /> <br /> Essentially, what Courts do is let the Court members choose the rules of engagement. The Fae (and by extension, the Huntsmen) have to play by Arcadian rules. Courts basically make those rules, in flesh space. So, when the Huntsmen are out of the Hedge, they have to abide by those rules. That's why Courts exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:51:54-08:00","id":387536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387381#post387381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the custom court idea. The Courts of Manhattan are Bull and Bear, changing power with the economy. The courts of Washington DC are an alphabet soup of changeling &amp;quot;agencies&amp;quot; that have a complicated bureaucratic structure adjusting their authority; or maybe there is the court of the Elephant and the court of the Donkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd avoid having just two Courts, the bare minimum I'd go for is three. That changes the dynamic a little bit more to avoid an us vs them type scenario. That said, though are both great ideas! Maybe add the a court of the Eagle to the Elephant and Donkey that takes power during election years, or when one party controls the Presidency and the other the Houses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T13:48:19-08:00","id":387601,"title":"","content":"I love this discussion about Courts )particularly the &quot;rules of engagement&quot; observation) and I hate to derail it, but I've been dying to ask about Talecrafting. I haven't noticed it in the outlines yet, and it seems to have taken a backseat to Oneiromancy and Pledges. Is it sort of related to the Court system, or are we going to get a completely new concept for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T16:01:05-08:00","id":387727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387601#post387601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this discussion about Courts )particularly the &quot;rules of engagement&quot; observation) and I hate to derail it, but I've been dying to ask about Talecrafting. I haven't noticed it in the outlines yet, and it seems to have taken a backseat to Oneiromancy and Pledges. Is it sort of related to the Court system, or are we going to get a completely new concept for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll probably be related to the Court system. Not sure yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T18:10:23-08:00","id":387894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387727#post387727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'll probably be related to the Court system. Not sure yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of things potentially related to the Court system: are Entitlements/Noble Orders somewhere on the docket, or will those presumably have to wait until e.g. pledges and such are sorted out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T19:38:50-08:00","id":387928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387894#post387894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of things potentially related to the Court system: are Entitlements/Noble Orders somewhere on the docket, or will those presumably have to wait until e.g. pledges and such are sorted out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Little bit of column A, little bit of column B. <br /> <br /> Not sure if we'll have space to do them justice in the core. Like with bloodlines in Requiem. Let me see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:22:41-08:00","id":388059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386931#post386931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: The issue with Pledges. As one of my friends puts it, &quot;There is no reason any Changeling should be poor.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I doubt that's changing, since one can say the exact same thing about demons, and in fact if memory serves demons are better at it than changelings are, so I don't see much nerfing coming changelings way, I'd be surprised if they didn't likewise become better at it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:05:04-08:00","id":388151,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's fair to say demons are better at it than changelings (at least 1e ones). Take a Greater Curse and Greater Alliance, and you can get a Lifetime Greater Boon. That's just one pledge, to one other individual. Make it your fellow Motley mate (aka another PC) and boom, Resources for no XP as long as the Motley is super loyal to each other.<br /> <br /> A Demon can't just make Resources out of nothing. They've got to find people with Resources, convince them to pact, and then use pacts to get things. Even then any Merits gained are tied to their Covers, which can be degraded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T02:24:39-08:00","id":388177,"title":"","content":"The only thing I really wanted from CtL 1e that wasn't addressed was further Courts, and any commentary on how universal the Seasonal and Directional Courts are. Color me a happy camper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T06:11:16-08:00","id":388370,"title":"","content":"The more I think about the information on the new Courts and their reasons for existing, the more the House Of Ballads from Kingdoms Of Amalur Reckoning pops up first in my head. And I mean this in an entirely good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:59:18-08:00","id":389178,"title":"","content":"Given that I live in the GTA (Greater Toronto Area) and have had some very fun times with some gorgeous Persian Woman (for the love of all that is whole don't use the term Iranian, its unsexy and Persian just sounds cooler, I mean no one say Iranian Rugs, they call them Persian Rugs).<br /> <br /> I also find the idea of setting up a Arabian 1001 nights theme in a City where I once had to shove 40cm of snow, to be weirdly fun. You end up in a blizzard, accidentally enter the hedge, and find yourself in a Sandstorm instead. Maybe the CN tower and Skydome are Palaces hedge side for the Courts. <br /> <br /> The Question given that Persians and Arabs, are minorities in Toronto, you have to answer why would the rest of the areas Changeling go with thier Court System and not say Native American, or English, or French, for example.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Previous Courts all fell before the Huntsmen, and so everyone backs the Persian Courts because they've survived when others fell, or perhaps Toronto simply didn't have enough Changelings prior to an influence of Persian Changelings, to establish a Court System, or it could he simply that Toronto's Changelings wanted to do something unexpected to throw the Huntment off.<br /> <br /> PS what happened to Hobgoblins, did the Hedge become uninhabited or are Hobgoblins not concidered anatogonists anymore, but local flora and fauna instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T18:04:06-08:00","id":389181,"title":"","content":"There is a reason for Changelings to be poor, 1. The Changeling is afraid of Pledges or doesn't believe in them, 2. The Changeling has taken an Oath of Poverty 3. The Changeling fears having money will make them easier to find and being poor will make them less memorable, so they choose greater anyonomity over money. 4. The Changeling lives a life style where money isn't important, say a Darkling that likes to live in the sewers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T18:11:01-08:00","id":389188,"title":"","content":"There are certainly reasons for Changelings to be poor. But, barring settings wherein its established that those who make Pledges for money are more likely to be found than those without them, poor Changelings are going to be the minority and the exception. Resources just gives you so many more options for running and hiding, even if you don't really need money for its own sake. It helps to set up and stock safe houses, create cover identities, bribe people to run interference for you, and a myriad other options that being poor doesn't allow.<br /> <br /> It's a bit odd though, because a culture of outsiders throwing around cash like it's nothing doesn't quite gel with the general feel of Changeling. Heck, I once played in a game where the GM had the Freehold create its own currency, because mortal money was considered near value-less for Changeling-to-Changeling dealings on account of how simple it is to generate from thin air and he wanted to enforce a sense of relative poverty for the lower level Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T19:32:01-08:00","id":389315,"title":"","content":"I've been reading up on the 1001 Nights, and it has Persian, East Indian, Eygptian, Mesopamion, Arab, Islamic, Jewish, Buddist, Hindu, Christian Influence, and hits upon many different parts of the world and beyond. So it fits a multicultural city like Toronto very well (plus it seems that the 1001 nights isn't popular in the Islamic World ironically as it is in the West).<br /> <br /> Some of the Stories are erotic, others are horror, and so on.<br /> <br /> But the key most universal themes appear to be Story Framing, as in stories within storiesn and fate destiny, both of which should have a key place in shaping Toronto's (assuming you don't change your mind) Courts. The first Framing Story is about King who kills his first wife for infidelity, then marries abunch of virgins and kills them too in the morning before they can betray him. Finally he marries the Vizars daughter who starts telling him a story that she doesn't finish, so the King spares her life long enough for her to tell him finish the story the next night, only for that to lead into another story, which also ends in a cliff hanger, and so this continues for 1001 nights, ending with the King deciding to spare her life.<br /> <br /> The King sounds like something a True Fae would do, sociopathically killing his wife, until one begins to tell him stories. Maybe the local courts try and distract the fae via story telling of this type like the Vizer's Daughter.<br /> <br /> Maybe each court could be based on a prefered genre of story telling, like one court is devoted to Erotic Tales, another Horror, another Comedy, another religious/philosphical tales, tradegy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T19:39:42-08:00","id":389325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=389315#post389315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading up on the 1001 Nights, and it has Persian, East Indian, Eygptian, Mesopamion, Arab, Islamic, Jewish, Buddist, Hindu, Christian Influence, and hits upon many different parts of the world and beyond. So it fits a multicultural city like Toronto very well (plus it seems that the 1001 nights isn't popular in the Islamic World ironically as it is in the West).<br /> <br /> Some of the Stories are erotic, others are horror, and so on.<br /> <br /> But the key most universal themes appear to be Story Framing, as in stories within storiesn and fate destiny, both of which should have a key place in shaping Toronto's (assuming you don't change your mind) Courts. The first Framing Story is about King who kills his first wife for infidelity, then marries abunch of virgins and kills them too in the morning before they can betray him. Finally he marries the Vizars daughter who starts telling him a story that she doesn't finish, so the King spares her life long enough for her to tell him finish the story the next night, only for that to lead into another story, which also ends in a cliff hanger, and so this continues for 1001 nights, ending with the King deciding to spare her life.<br /> <br /> The King sounds like something a True Fae would do, sociopathically killing his wife, until one begins to tell him stories. Maybe the local courts try and distract the fae via story telling of this type like the Vizer's Daughter.<br /> <br /> Maybe each court could be based on a prefered genre of story telling, like one court is devoted to Erotic Tales, another Horror, another Comedy, another religious/philosphical tales, tradegy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a really cool take on it. I'll tell Marianne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T19:51:56-08:00","id":389331,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the more it could work.<br /> Functional Scheherazade (the Changelings), distracts Sultan*Shahriyar (the True Fae) so that they will be spared with stories and tales of all sorts.<br /> <br /> So to fight the huntsmen, a Changeling might in a seasonal court only be hunted during thier season, or be spared if the Changeling can insight thier emotion in the huntsmen without magic, but in these Persian/Canadian courts you might tell the huntsmen a tale, which leads to another tale, until you escape, or the huntsman or a 1001 nights have past.<br /> <br /> and like I said basing the courts around genres of story told makes it easy to link them to emotions for glamour harevesting, erotic arousal, horror fear, comedy humour, spiritual faith, tragedy sadness.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that the heads of the courts will be called Sultans, or Sultana if female?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:05:26-08:00","id":389340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=389325#post389325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be a really cool take on it. I'll tell Marianne.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T20:10:25-08:00","id":389344,"title":"","content":"Heck 1001 nights even has fantasy/science fiction elements with robots and sorcerors and the like (i kid you not robots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T01:02:20-08:00","id":389529,"title":"","content":"Now I;m wondering if goblin vows are going to be included in the 2d ed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T06:29:03-08:00","id":389767,"title":"","content":"Goblin vows might be a merit or added directly to the Pledge section. Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:14:37-08:00","id":390980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387727#post387727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'll probably be related to the Court system. Not sure yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope this can be taken as an implication that Talecrafting will get some kind of mention in the book (I can't remember if you said anything on it's inclusion before). Talecrafting is one of my favorite systems in Changeling, and I'd hate for it to get left behind with the shift to 2e. Especially with the additional focus on 'stories' in the new edition, which makes Talecrafting in some form even more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I LOVE said additional focus on 'stories.' The fact the Wyrd has always effectively been a Law of Narrative Casualty was something implied in the original 1e book, but it wasn't until Sword at Dawn I felt the concept really came into it's own. Other splats have taken notice, from what I've seen of the other 2e books. The Arcanthus Mage preview shows they're working a bit more closely with the Law of Narrative Casualty the Wyrd represents. The Cahalith preview for Werewolf demonstrates a similar emphasis on 'stories'.<br /> <br /> So seeing Changeling, where it all began, embrace the concept makes me all the more excited for the book.<br /> <br /> The other thing I'm looking forward to is the 'mortal splat'. Now, this had been something I'd been wondering about. Unlike Vampire (ghouls), Werewolf (wolf-blooded), and Mage (Proximi/Sleepwalkers), Changeling lacked any real 'halfway' minor template/minor supernatural Merit that could be fleshed out and expanded upon. The closest was the Fae-Touched in Equinox Roads, but one look at how they form (escaped Arcadia before the process of becoming changelings was complete) should tell you how unreasonable it was for them to fulfill the same role ghouls, wolf-blooded, and Sleepwalkers/Proximi fill.<br /> <br /> But it looks like you're creating a minor template whole cloth for Changeling. I can't wait to see what you guys cook up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:03:45-08:00","id":391036,"title":"","content":"I always felt Ensorcelled Mortals filled the &quot;mortal splat&quot; role. Could be bound to serve, showered with merits to a much greater extent than Changelings, and had a variety of useful applications for their Changeling masters (with an appropriately worded pledge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:22:25-08:00","id":391048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=391036#post391036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt Ensorcelled Mortals filled the &quot;mortal splat&quot; role. Could be bound to serve, showered with merits to a much greater extent than Changelings, and had a variety of useful applications for their Changeling masters (with an appropriately worded pledge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, ensorcellement (to my knowledge) almost always required a pledge. If there was, say, a Merit option to be permanently ensorcelled with a pledge, or a way to become permanently ensorcelled without ending up in Arcadia, they maybe. But there wasn't, and as it stands an enscorcelled mortal simply couldn't be 'fleshed out' to fill the role needed for the 'mortal splat'.<br /> <br /> It's hard to articulate. Ensorcellement was a boon granted by a pledge (usually), nothing more. For it to gain additional powers and reach the level of other minor templates, it would require a significant re-working of ensorcellement. It certainly wouldn't be something granted by a simple pledge like in 1e. And the ability to simply grant someone the ability to see through the Mask via pledge is simply too useful, and critical, for it to come with additional supernatural baggage.<br /> <br /> The developers are making the right move making a whole new mortal splat. I assume the splat is ensorcelled themselves, or will have a way of looking through the Mask, in order to fill the needed role in changeling society. In other words, the mortal splat likely will be an ensorcelled mortal, in the technical sense. But simply being able to see through the Mask a splat does not make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:36:04-08:00","id":391055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alisa180</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=391048#post391048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, ensorcellement (to my knowledge) almost always required a pledge. If there was, say, a Merit option to be permanently ensorcelled with a pledge, or a way to become permanently ensorcelled without ending up in Arcadia, they maybe. But there wasn't, and as it stands an enscorcelled mortal simply couldn't be 'fleshed out' to fill the role needed for the 'mortal splat'.<br /> <br /> It's hard to articulate. Ensorcellement was a boon granted by a pledge (usually), nothing more. For it to gain additional powers and reach the level of other minor templates, it would require a significant re-working of ensorcellement. It certainly wouldn't be something granted by a simple pledge like in 1e. And the ability to simply grant someone the ability to see through the Mask via pledge is simply too useful, and critical, for it to come with additional supernatural baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll here point out that despite my readthrough of 1e being much delayed by detours through other books, both the 1e core and Autumn Nightmares provide narrative basis for an &quot;ensorcelled template&quot; via things like eternal ensorcellment through exposure to the magic of the Wyrd and dream-warping allowing the Fae to give &quot;truly favored&quot; ensorcelled mortals the use of their Contracts at the cost of their sanity.<br /> <br /> That and the poisoning of the boon of ensorcellment seemed like one of maybe three good reasons to tie the quality to finite-duration pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:03:27-08:00","id":391486,"title":"","content":"I already wrote this on this page (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-kickstarter-is-live/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/world-of-dark...arter-is-live/</a>), but by know I got the impression that it was the wrong place. Sadly I can't delete it myself... <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I made some research by myself about the more original fairy tales and decided to share some of it with you for &quot;Changeling: The Lost&quot;. The first thing you should know is, that there is not &quot;one&quot; true original you can refer to. These tales where told from one person to another and so a lot of different versions exist. Some of them are very very old and go back to the middle age or even the 10th century.<br /> The brothers Grimm were one of the first people, that decided to collect them and write them down. They made a trip across Germany and asked local people to tell them these stories. Their route is still well know. Translated it would mean something like &quot;The German Fairy Tale Route&quot;. <br /> Their first version from 1810 was never published, it was crueler than their later version for children, but also not always as cruel as some other (usually older) version. (As far as I could find out...). <br /> <br /> So referring to the Grimm tales as THE original is simply wrong! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here you can read about some significant differences of a few tales to the published version of the brothers Grimm for children. I did not write the following myself, but collected the most important parts from a few sources in English instead of translating the German ones to save some time:<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Little Red Riding Hood</b><br /> <br /> These early variations of the tale differ from the currently known version in several ways. The antagonist is not always a wolf, but sometimes an ogre or a 'bzou' (werewolf), making these tales relevant to the werewolf-trials (similar to witch trials) of the time (e.g. the trial of Peter Stumpp). The wolf usually leaves the grandmother\u2019s blood and meat for the girl to eat, who then unwittingly cannibalizes her own grandmother. Furthermore, the wolf was also known to ask her to remove her clothing and toss it into the fire. In some versions, the wolf eats the girl after she gets into bed with him, and the story ends there.<br /> <br /> Source:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Riding_Hood\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_J._W._Smith.jpg/960px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_J._W._Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Riding_Hood\" target=\"_blank\"> Little Red Riding Hood - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Riding_Hood\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Riding_Hood </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Older versions of the tale:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.furorteutonicus.eu/germanic/ashliman/mirror/type0333.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.furorteutonicus.eu/germanic/ashliman/mirror/type0333.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.furorteutonicus.eu/germanic/ashliman/mirror/type0333.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.furorteutonicus.eu/germanic/ashliman/mirror/type0333.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Sleeping Beauty</b><br /> <br /> In the original story of Sleeping Beauty she falls asleep due to a prophesy, not a curse. Guess what? It isn\u2019t a kiss from a prince that wakes her either. In fact there is no prince at all in the original story of Sleeping Beauty. The king sees Sleeping Beauty and decides to rape her! She has two babies nine months later, even while she is still sleeping. She awakes when one of the children sucks a piece of flux off her finger that was causing her to sleep only to discover she had been raped and is now the mother of two children.<br /> <br /> Source:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://unrealfacts.com/sleeping-beauty-was-a-rape-victim-in-the-original-story/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://unrealfacts.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/site-logo2-210x57.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unrealfacts.com/sleeping-beauty-was-a-rape-victim-in-the-original-story/\" target=\"_blank\"> Sleeping Beauty Was a Rape Victim in the Original Story - Unreal Facts for Amazing facts </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unrealfacts.com/sleeping-beauty-was-a-rape-victim-in-the-original-story/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://unrealfacts.com/sleeping-beauty-was-a-rape-victim-in-the-original-story/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sleeping beauty really was raped! Click here to find out who the offender was. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Snow White</b><br /> <br /> The cannibal Queen<br /> In the newer version, the cannibalistic action of the Stepmother is not mentioned. In the earlier version, the Stepmother orders the huntsman to kill Snow White and bring the girl\u2019s lungs and liver, not only as proof that she is dead but also to be eaten.<br /> <br /> The necrophiliac Prince<br /> In the newer version Snow White is awaken when the Prince kisses her. In the original version, there is no kiss. The Prince insists in having the coffin. Then, he asks his men to carry the coffin with the girl\u2019s lifeless body in it. When the men carrying the coffin stumble over some rock, the poisonous apple comes out of her throat and Snow White is once more alive. What does the Prince want with a dead girl\u2019s body? In the original version, not only is he a pedophile but a necrophiliac as well. The fact that the seven dwarfs refuse to bury the girl and instead keep her in a glass coffin so that they can stare at her is already disturbing. The desire of the Prince to have the body adds to the horrifying aspect of this original version.<br /> <br /> Source:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://yovitasiswati.expertscolumn.com/article/snow-white-canibal-queen-and-necrophiliac-prince\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://expertscolumn.com/image_files/thumbmain/\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://yovitasiswati.expertscolumn.com/article/snow-white-canibal-queen-and-necrophiliac-prince\" target=\"_blank\"> Snow White : The Canibal Queen And Necrophiliac Prince </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://yovitasiswati.expertscolumn.com/article/snow-white-canibal-queen-and-necrophiliac-prince\" target=\"_blank\"> http://yovitasiswati.expertscolumn.com/article/snow-white-canibal-queen-and-necrophiliac-prince </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Snow White is a sweet story of an innocent girl fighting for her life. Do you know that the original version of Snow White fairytale is full of shocking plots?The Grimm&rsquo;s collection is our only source of the original version of the story as Perrault did not include Snow White in his collection. Grimm made two versions. The first was recorded in 1810 and known as the &ldquo;peasant version&rdquo;. In this first version there were no stepmother and prince. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Maybe it's too much to ask, but I would be happy, if you would include some of those versions, when you talk about the original versions in your next &quot;Changeling: The Lost&quot; books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:27:32-08:00","id":391617,"title":"","content":"Have you, um, read the Seemings and Kiths in the 1e corebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:39:28-08:00","id":391759,"title":"","content":"One aspect which was barely touched in <i>the Lost</i> was the effects of long term feeding on humans. I wonder if in the new version changelings will be more like emotion vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:20:05-08:00","id":391924,"title":"","content":"They also had Cambions as a Mortal Splat, but Cambions were more the mortal splat for Succubi then Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T17:17:47-08:00","id":392057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=391486#post391486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's too much to ask, but I would be happy, if you would include some of those versions, when you talk about the original versions in your next &quot;Changeling: The Lost&quot; books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We won't do a lot of talking about specific stories. We'll do subtle callouts in Kiths and Seemings. But I prefer to keep the opportunities open. This isn't a game about fairy tales; it's a game about Changelings in the modern world. <br /> <br /> That said, we WILL be referencing Grimm's versions of the stories in the Dark Eras supplement we're doing. But that's nothing to do with originality; it's everything to do with massive proliferation of so many stories all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T03:03:12-08:00","id":392479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=392057#post392057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We won't do a lot of talking about specific stories. We'll do subtle callouts in Kiths and Seemings. But I prefer to keep the opportunities open. This isn't a game about fairy tales; it's a game about Changelings in the modern world. <br /> <br /> That said, we WILL be referencing Grimm's versions of the stories in the Dark Eras supplement we're doing. But that's nothing to do with originality; it's everything to do with massive proliferation of so many stories all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Maybe you misunderstood what I meant, because there are really a lot of fairy tale examples and references throughout the whole 1e. Especially in &quot;Swords at Dawn&quot; and also the inspired antagonists in &quot;Grim Fears&quot;. And those are the things I am talking about. Nothing more! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And because of that the 1e always made the impression to be a setting for some kind of modern, scary fairy tales, too. And that's one of the things I liked about it the most. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So I hope the 2e will keep that up.<br /> <br /> By the way I would like to know, if possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , whether the Huntsman are also part of the Wild Hunt, or whether these are two completely different things!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-04-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T04:10:54-08:00","id":392501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=391055#post391055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll here point out that despite my readthrough of 1e being much delayed by detours through other books, both the 1e core and Autumn Nightmares provide narrative basis for an &quot;ensorcelled template&quot; via things like eternal ensorcellment through exposure to the magic of the Wyrd and dream-warping allowing the Fae to give &quot;truly favored&quot; ensorcelled mortals the use of their Contracts at the cost of their sanity.<br /> <br /> That and the poisoning of the boon of ensorcellment seemed like one of maybe three good reasons to tie the quality to finite-duration pledges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that &quot;super Ensorcelled&quot; is the way to go with Mortal Template. Maybe something like humans that are granted part of Wyrd of Changeling they are created from? Or Ensorcelled that are sustained by the Glamour they are &quot;feed&quot; by the Lost - like vampires are feeding Ghouls. Of course, those &quot;super Ensorcelled&quot; will probably need other name for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T10:15:41-08:00","id":392676,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering how powerful are contracts going to be? I mean if you've seen my opinion of them so far you know I can be pretty abrasive when it comes to them but I'm hoping they'll get buffed to be more closer to other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T10:53:15-08:00","id":392721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=392676#post392676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering how powerful are contracts going to be? I mean if you've seen my opinion of them so far you know I can be pretty abrasive when it comes to them but I'm hoping they'll get buffed to be more closer to other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>David chimed in on this a little earlier, though I know I'd love a clearer idea about the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=386945#post386945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are contract going to get a power up?<br /> i had a reality shock when i started to play changeling after having played vampire and mage because, for example, while i could rule in social interactions with dominate, majesty and mind arcanum, vainglory felt like just a few bonus and tricks, nothing to big</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=387120#post387120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There will be some shift there. But, that's not the place you're going to see the biggest change in basic edges. Changelings will be a little different on a template level.<br /> <br /> They will be able to flip the proverbial table. But, in that case, it's going to be a question of &quot;should they?&quot; Because, you know, consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be interested in sharing a little more about where Changelings will have this extra muscle to flex, David? Shot in the dark, maybe some connection to the Durance-related rituals they can perform? Or is it somewhat like the idea I always heard talked about for 1e, where they're encouraged to &quot;stack the deck&quot; to come out on top?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T12:11:59-08:00","id":392845,"title":"","content":"If I had my guess it has to do with getting people caught in the Changelings Story, talecrafting in otherwords and perhaps pledges.<br /> <br /> In fact perhaps the mortal splat are simply humans who have somehow gotten caught up in the Changeling story and as such have thier fate/wyrd altered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:06:30-08:00","id":392916,"title":"","content":"To exand on my point just as Huntsmen have to obey the rules of the Changelings narritive in the mortal world, especially that of the courts and possibly noble/eldrich entitlements, perhaps in thier own way some mortals, especially those close to a changeling, motley, or court, get caught up in thier own way, becoming characters in the story and being shaped by it, the side effect of which is it changes them, ensorcelles them and gives them access to certain abilities and fey magic. A Storytouched Mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:27:30-08:00","id":392952,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like Hedge Witches from the fanon <i>Wyrd Sorcery</i>, who gain their power from a Pledge with a True Fae (with themselves or their ancestors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:32:32-08:00","id":393862,"title":"","content":"Will second edition describe, how many changellings live in the world in average?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:42:13-08:00","id":393870,"title":"","content":"Never.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:57:00-08:00","id":393899,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it bothers me enough that some of the other core books did that (roughly 100,000 werewolves world-wide?)<br /> <br /> Though I <i>did</i> like how in <i>To the Strongest</i> they pointed out that there are the same number of Awakened souls in Hellenistic Greece as there are in the modern day, either implying that the number of Awakened souls is constant or that the war between the Exarchs and the Pentacle hasn't progressed in either direction at all in <i>two millennia</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:20:46-08:00","id":393923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=393899#post393899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it bothers me enough that some of the other core books did that (roughly 100,000 werewolves world-wide?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Half a million.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, those statistics were handy for reminding yourself that the supernatural is not <i>unilaterally omnipresent</i>, but yeah, specific counts don't otherwise have a very high utility; things like &quot;some cities don't have any werewolves at all&quot; or &quot;the global Promethean population usually doesn't pass much higher than triple digits&quot; serve better, and for low-key groups like changelings and demons having a definite headcount raises a lot of needless questions of verifiability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:58:03-08:00","id":394206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=393862#post393862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will second edition describe, how many changellings live in the world in average?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. We might give examples of how many might exist in a small or large city Freehold. But I don't want to make sweeping statements like that without a super good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T16:20:07-08:00","id":394247,"title":"","content":"It's a particularly pointless distinction, I've always found, since Changeling population has never been tied to local human populations. More than any other World of Darkness creature, they embody the principle of &quot;there are as many as you need for the story&quot;. Like, to the point that it's actually almost implied to be an in-universe law. A small country town could have a Changeling population that dwarfs the population of New York, which I think is given as 37 in Lords of Summer. With the variation on the ground being so considerable, a world-wide population would be functionally useless. It provides no practical gauge at all for the purposes of building a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T09:07:30-08:00","id":394971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=393862#post393862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will second edition describe, how many changellings live in the world in average?</div> </div> </div> </div> Shudder. The only thing that ever served was for my players to complain about population ratios in my cities. I pray that never shows up in any of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T11:12:44-08:00","id":395165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=394971#post394971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Shudder. The only thing that ever served was for my players to complain about population ratios in my cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, what was up with that? Even around the statement in vampire it says that it's just an estimate and some are higher and lower, but a month can't go by without someone somewhere making a deal about how it doesn't make sense that there's x vampires in y when the population of y is z. Or lamenting their inability to do a small town chronicle because the book says there should only be 2 vampires there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:15:25-08:00","id":395758,"title":"","content":"Will legendary tokens be a thing in 2E? And for hedgespun, will it be broad-ranging with automatons and machines or purely equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:34:36-08:00","id":395769,"title":"","content":"It's a core book. Keep it simple and focused is probably the prevailing rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:10:49-08:00","id":396308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=395769#post395769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a core book. Keep it simple and focused is probably the prevailing rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. We're TIGHT on word count. Most things will only get the lightest touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T21:02:20-08:00","id":397152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=396308#post396308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. We're TIGHT on word count. Most things will only get the lightest touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, I noticed tightness was a <i>big</i> theme in the outline. As an admitted outsider, it continues to strike me as really ambitious to try to get in as much as you've planned.<br /> <br /> I know it may depend on a number of factors -- and this may not be the question to ask when the corebook itself is a ways out -- but are there any supplements you'd be really keen on doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T23:22:58-08:00","id":397236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=397152#post397152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aye, I noticed tightness was a <i>big</i> theme in the outline. As an admitted outsider, it continues to strike me as really ambitious to try to get in as much as you've planned.<br /> <br /> I know it may depend on a number of factors -- and this may not be the question to ask when the corebook itself is a ways out -- but are there any supplements you'd be really keen on doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. There's a few.<br /> <br /> But I can't talk about them. Unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:09:37-08:00","id":398731,"title":"","content":"Is there a chance that the book will get a deluxe edition by using a kickstarter for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:09:35-08:00","id":399134,"title":"","content":"Will we be seeing a deeper exploration of harvesting Glamour in