lways felt shallow to me in the original game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely, yes. Not sure exactly what's happening until first drafts are in. But I have faith in my author here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:29:09-08:00","id":403242,"title":"","content":"Do you know if Bedlam will be included in 2e, and if so, will it be expanded in any way? In the first edition, I don't recall it ever being mentioned in any Changeling book outside the small blurb in the core, the rules for which implied a certain reification of the Seasonal Courts. No one has ever used it in any game I've been in, and I can't quite figure out what symbolic space it's supposed to occupy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:35:36-08:00","id":403244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=403242#post403242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know if Bedlam will be included in 2e, and if so, will it be expanded in any way? In the first edition, I don't recall it ever being mentioned in any Changeling book outside the small blurb in the core, the rules for which implied a certain reification of the Seasonal Courts. No one has ever used it in any game I've been in, and I can't quite figure out what symbolic space it's supposed to occupy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't come up at all in our discussions. And I don't think it's ever come up in any of my tons of play. <br /> <br /> I think part of that is its mostly a thing for immensely high Wyrd characters. I don't find it particularly interesting as-is. If one of my writers wants to touch on it, that's cool. But, it's not a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T08:04:13-08:00","id":403329,"title":"","content":"Inflicting Bedlam does seem to have some parallels with Predatory Aura and Lashing Out with the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:26:50-08:00","id":404008,"title":"","content":"Honestly I liked inflicting bedlam, but it should come at the beginning, instead of higher Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:49:23-08:00","id":404021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=404008#post404008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I liked inflicting bedlam, but it should come at the beginning, instead of higher Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really really liked the idea! A good parallel indeed to the Nimbus and Predatory Aura rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T19:58:12-08:00","id":404027,"title":"","content":"I'm... away from my books and drawing a complete blank. &gt;.&gt; What is Bedlam in Changeling: the Lost 1e, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T20:13:49-08:00","id":404034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=404027#post404027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... away from my books and drawing a complete blank. &gt;.&gt; What is Bedlam in Changeling: the Lost 1e, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bedlam is essentially the ability to inflict a strong emotion from the Seasonal Courts' set of four on a large group of people with increasing frequency at Wyrd 6+, rolling Manipulation+Wyrd+[modifiers which include &quot;does this emotion correspond to your Court, your Court's 'opposite,' or one of the other two?&quot; and &quot;how fitting is this emotion to the context?&quot;].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T23:48:43-08:00","id":404178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=403329#post403329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inflicting Bedlam does seem to have some parallels with Predatory Aura and Lashing Out with the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would support &quot;Inflicting Bedlam as Aura&quot; mechanics in 2ed core. In much smaller scale, on personal level - but it has sense in the gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:16:58-08:00","id":404482,"title":"","content":"Bedlam isn't a complex detailed mechanic so it shouldn't be hard to include a version of Bedlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:26:54-08:00","id":404489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=404178#post404178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would support &quot;Inflicting Bedlam as Aura&quot; mechanics in 2ed core. In much smaller scale, on personal level - but it has sense in the gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be nice to have like a generic Bedlam that inflict the Lost madness on others and one tied to the emotions of the Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:42:45-08:00","id":404506,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about how they design courts and court contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:55:48-08:00","id":404517,"title":"","content":"Vishkanya would make for a cool Fairest Variant for Venombite Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:14:14-08:00","id":405392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=403244#post403244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It hasn't come up at all in our discussions. And I don't think it's ever come up in any of my tons of play.<br /> <br /> I think part of that is its mostly a thing for immensely high Wyrd characters. I don't find it particularly interesting as-is. If one of my writers wants to touch on it, that's cool. But, it's not a priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what is it that changelings get as an aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:37:39-08:00","id":405402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=405392#post405392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then what is it that changelings get as an aura?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantle, duh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:49:35-08:00","id":406648,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Kith, Olympians. <br /> <br /> A Greek God could be symbolic of each seeming.<br /> <br /> Fairest- Venus <br /> Orger- Ares<br /> Wizen- Hapheutuos <br /> Darkling- Hecate/Hades<br /> Beast- Pan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:43:45-08:00","id":407285,"title":"","content":"I noticed the outline has been update especially on the issue of who gets what contracts looks like their planning on having all of them, but instead of each being a group of 5 powers, it appears to be a single power per contract kind of like how some goblin contracts were. I wouldn't be surprised if some contracts powers end up as a seeming twist. <br /> <br /> Also noticed each city will get one or two contracts so it will be interesting to see how all the seasonal courts powers get shrunken down to one or two contract powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T23:16:27-08:00","id":408655,"title":"","content":"I didn't see a mention of Darklings in the Outline. Are they still in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T23:42:46-08:00","id":408661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=408655#post408655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see a mention of Darklings in the Outline. Are they still in?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll be present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:01:36-07:00","id":493710,"title":"","content":"I know I'm late to asking questions here, but since I have the, I thought I'd ask:<br /> <br /> <b>Oneiromancy</b><br /> <br /> Since my players have loved it over the years but we've had to adjust it a lot, I thought I'd ask about it.<br /> <br /> Can we have groups of maneuvers (like analysis, manipulation, healing) and rolls determined by the category? Something to streamline the rolls but not have it all be Wits + Empathy + Wyrd?<br /> <br /> Will there be an option and rules for for entering dreams as a group, perhaps through skeinwalking?<br /> <br /> <b>Pledges</b><br /> <br /> Can an option for more freeform pledges be worked into a later supplement, perhaps? Because while the old system took some getting used to, it offers a lot of flexibility that some players really enjoy. Since the new edition seems focused on offering players a lot of options to choose from, it seems natural that pledges could be thus. Perhaps in an advanced form? Will there be a roll for pledge-making, and/or a system for those who try to deceive while setting up pledges?<br /> <br /> Will there be a curse system, perhaps as an advanced pledge variation? A number of fairy tales are about levying curses out of spite, which would make excellent Conditions and stories but would need rules to avoid major abuses.<br /> <br /> <b>Fetches</b><br /> <br /> Can we have a system for more advanced fetches and/or ways to make them scarier antagonists?<br /> <br /> <b>Misc</b>.<br /> <br /> I saw a section for goblin fruit. Will there still be trifles and oddments, or is it all under the banner of goblin fruit now? <br /> <br /> Similarly, will there be more of a structure for the various types of creatures in the game and building them with some additional guidancee? It seemed like it might be easier to have a basic template for each major type (hedge-warped, Arcadian native, incubi or dream-natives) that could then be added to based upon the Wyrd rating of a particular creature. <br /> <br /> Are there any plans to tackle the Hedge in greater depth and length?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:50:32-07:00","id":494137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=493710#post493710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm late to asking questions here, but since I have the, I thought I'd ask:<br /> <br /> <b>Oneiromancy</b><br /> <br /> Since my players have loved it over the years but we've had to adjust it a lot, I thought I'd ask about it.<br /> <br /> Can we have groups of maneuvers (like analysis, manipulation, healing) and rolls determined by the category? Something to streamline the rolls but not have it all be Wits + Empathy + Wyrd?<br /> <br /> Will there be an option and rules for for entering dreams as a group, perhaps through skeinwalking?<br /> <br /> <b>Pledges</b><br /> <br /> Can an option for more freeform pledges be worked into a later supplement, perhaps? Because while the old system took some getting used to, it offers a lot of flexibility that some players really enjoy. Since the new edition seems focused on offering players a lot of options to choose from, it seems natural that pledges could be thus. Perhaps in an advanced form? Will there be a roll for pledge-making, and/or a system for those who try to deceive while setting up pledges?<br /> <br /> Will there be a curse system, perhaps as an advanced pledge variation? A number of fairy tales are about levying curses out of spite, which would make excellent Conditions and stories but would need rules to avoid major abuses.<br /> <br /> <b>Fetches</b><br /> <br /> Can we have a system for more advanced fetches and/or ways to make them scarier antagonists?<br /> <br /> <b>Misc</b>.<br /> <br /> I saw a section for goblin fruit. Will there still be trifles and oddments, or is it all under the banner of goblin fruit now?<br /> <br /> Similarly, will there be more of a structure for the various types of creatures in the game and building them with some additional guidancee? It seemed like it might be easier to have a basic template for each major type (hedge-warped, Arcadian native, incubi or dream-natives) that could then be added to based upon the Wyrd rating of a particular creature.<br /> <br /> Are there any plans to tackle the Hedge in greater depth and length?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plans to tackle the Hedge in greater depth and length. Oh yes, there are. <br /> <br /> Oneiromancy: I haven't read the draft yet, but I did give it a bigger focus in this book. <br /> <br /> Pledges: We have a whole new pledge system. I think it's awesome. I think you'll think it's awesome. <br /> <br /> Fetches: Matt McFarland wrote them in the supplements. I gave him free reign in the core here. I think they're going to be great. <br /> <br /> Goblin Fruit: Right now, they're all under one banner. It's a short section. I didn't want to bog it down. I may elaborate later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T21:15:06-07:00","id":494344,"title":"","content":"I did touch on Bedlam, yes, but like many, it almost never comes up in my games. I made it slightly more accessible, but maybe didn't go far enough. A full-on aura effect could be fun, but we'll see what happens behind the scenes. I don't want to touch too much on it.<br /> <br /> Glamour harvesting I was quite happy with, but we'll see what happens there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T00:54:07-07:00","id":494500,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of not every Fetch being an antagonist, personally. Of course they're out there and living your character's life, though that alone shouldn't make them a baddy to be smashed to their requisite bits and pieces.<br /> One game I played had my changeling on the hunt for his Fetch, only to find an old man with a terminal illness in a hospital bed... Took the adrenaline of a scrap right out the moment, but having my changeling sit by the bed of this dying man suffering from Alzheimers and watching him as he went naturally... It was strong stuff.<br /> <br /> I can see other Fetches not wanting to fight or trying to somehow make amends with the changeling for their role in their abduction. For me even the Loyalists and Privateers have their sides to them, the Loyalists are mostly hopelessly mad and the Privateers may be scared silly of their Keeper and hate what they are behind closed doors but have no choice but to continue doing what they do.<br /> <br /> Thats just what kinds of things happen in my changeling universe, I'm glad to see the Huntsmen, they seem really cool. I'd like to know more about them, whether they're some kind of Hob, a knowing agent for the Keeper or perhaps something far more Cthulhuesque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:41:35-07:00","id":494951,"title":"","content":"Not every fetch has to be an antagonist, but it would be nice to have some tiered options for threat level for those who are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:46:21-07:00","id":495061,"title":"","content":"Remember that &quot;antagonist&quot; doesn't mean &quot;thing you have to kill&quot;. It means a problem for your outlook and approach to life. It means something if you resolve that problem by killing it, or by making peace, or by mutual avoidance, or by some disturbing twin-brothers con-game, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:39:54-07:00","id":495138,"title":"","content":"*nods* Yes, I realise my wording was probably somewhat off in the point I was trying to get across. Btw I totally agree having some more info on Fetches would be awesome. Because sometimes I've played Changeling and honestly forgot about them. They make a fair subject for Aspirations I would think if worded right but having them more at the fore, whether an enemy or merely something that interacts more directly than present into Changeling existance would be good.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a Changeling and Fetch are linked more overtly in the dreamscape, a little like the Dreamsharing Bestowment in Promethean? Or some other way that makes them hard to avoid for the Changeling as they go about their business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:36:47-07:00","id":496198,"title":"","content":"Just a little question, we have seen the roles that Kith and Seeming play in 2ed(and they seen really awesome!) and we also know Courts will be present.<br /> But what about Entitlements, are they still a thing in 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:00:32-07:00","id":496209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=496198#post496198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a little question, we have seen the roles that Kith and Seeming play in 2ed(and they seen really awesome!) and we also know Courts will be present.<br /> But what about Entitlements, are they still a thing in 2ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entitlements won't be appearing in detail in 2e's core. For the same reasons Bloodlines aren't in Requiem 2e. BUT, we already have a couple of sample Entitlements planned, which will go into Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T08:36:20-07:00","id":496330,"title":"","content":"What I'd like to see for fetches is the option of giving them Kiths (but not Seemings).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:59:26-07:00","id":496927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=496209#post496209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entitlements won't be appearing in detail in 2e's core. For the same reasons Bloodlines aren't in Requiem 2e. BUT, we already have a couple of sample Entitlements planned, which will go into Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great to know, thanks!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:39:02-07:00","id":497108,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in just how changelings can have a Kith but no Seeming, as hinted at before. I'd have thought even Loyalists and Privateers got to reality in some manner, even if it wasn't a true escape, they've actively changed their stance and returned to reality, still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:58:14-07:00","id":497121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497108#post497108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in just how changelings can have a Kith but no Seeming, as hinted at before. I'd have thought even Loyalists and Privateers got to reality in some manner, even if it wasn't a true escape, they've actively changed their stance and returned to reality, still.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems less about getting back to the mortal world and more about agency. When a mortal is taken and made into a Changeling, that character acquires a Kith as one of the Gentry (or Arcadia itself) remakes her, creating a new role to force on her and thereby remove her agency. Her life was her story, but meaningful control over it has been taken from her: her Keeper is telling it now.<br /> <br /> If and when she takes back that agency and makes the story of her life her own to tell, usually as part of escaping the one who kept her agency from her, she develops a Seeming to reflect the manner in which she did so. If she didn't take her life back, returning to the mortal world by whatever other means won't grant her a Seeming.<br /> <br /> It's not really clear to us at this point if a Changeling can develop a Seeming after leaving Arcadia. It could be that taking her life back whenever is enough for a Seeming, or it could be that Arcadia's narrative bent is the only sort of place where that Changeling's self-determination can remake her with a Seeming. Or, obviously, other options not thought up or identified here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:11:31-07:00","id":497127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If she didn't take her life back, returning to the mortal world by whatever other means won't grant her a Seeming. </div> </div> </div>I see. But still, I'd have thought escaping and leaving that life behind would be the first move to agency and so would get a Seeming. I suppose I might need an example of a changeling escaping Arcadia but not regaining that agency to really grok how that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:26:31-07:00","id":497131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497127#post497127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. But still, I'd have thought escaping and leaving that life behind would be the first move to agency and so would get a Seeming. I suppose I might need an example of a changeling escaping Arcadia but not regaining that agency to really grok how that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Escape&quot; is a verb in the active voice, and not one mutually inclusive with all means of winding up in the mortal world.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if you're familiar with Demon, but gaining Seeming in 2e appears to be loosely analogous to the Fall \u2014 it doesn't happen just because your Lord or Lady accidentally swept you under the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-30-2015, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T00:51:01-07:00","id":497210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497131#post497131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Escape&quot; is a verb in the active voice, and not one mutually inclusive with all means of winding up in the mortal world.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if you're familiar with Demon, but gaining Seeming in 2e appears to be loosely analogous to the Fall \u2014 it doesn't happen just because your Lord or Lady accidentally swept you under the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you arranged the &quot;accident&quot;, in which case Darkling seeming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:06:36-07:00","id":497862,"title":"","content":"One question that's crossed my mind. So courts are becoming a lot less formal in 2e. Rather than the traditional seasonal courts, those will just be an example of numerous different court structures freeholds can use.<br /> <br /> Of course this raises the question, if there's no set court system and people are encouraged to build their own, does that mean there won't be court contracts? That would be somewhat disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:41:18-07:00","id":497894,"title":"","content":"The outline includes Court Contracts as being a thing still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T16:33:51-07:00","id":497983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497894#post497894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The outline includes Court Contracts as being a thing still.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll exist. But I should probably note, there won't be quite as many because we're not using 1-5 tiered powers. This actually facilitates there being Court Contracts, though. With the longer form, I couldn't fit so many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:38:31-07:00","id":498185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497131#post497131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Escape&quot; is a verb in the active voice, and not one mutually inclusive with all means of winding up in the mortal world.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if you're familiar with Demon, but gaining Seeming in 2e appears to be loosely analogous to the Fall \u2014 it doesn't happen just because your Lord or Lady accidentally swept you under the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm familiar with Demon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay, so that makes more sense now. So would be correct to think that those without Seemings can perhaps be something akin to Exiles from D:tD? I see those without Seemings being more Privateers than anything else atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:15:17-07:00","id":505741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=497983#post497983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'll exist. But I should probably note, there won't be quite as many because we're not using 1-5 tiered powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... What are you using? From the outline, it looks to me like something closer to Transmutations from <b>Promethean: the Created</b>\u2014a kind of 'pick-and-choose' from the various levels\u2014than the 'tiered powers' that we already know, but it's not quite clear. Of course, it could well be something that you're not ready to unveil, but it sounds like a pretty major change to the core mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:17:09-07:00","id":505742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=505741#post505741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... What are you using? From the outline, it looks to me like something closer to Transmutations from <b>Promethean: the Created</b>\u2014a kind of 'pick-and-choose' from the various levels\u2014than the 'tiered powers' that we already know, but it's not quite clear. Of course, it could well be something that you're not ready to unveil, but it sounds like a pretty major change to the core mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>They look a little like Gifts in Forsaken 2e. A little. <br /> <br /> Basically, they're individual powers, which have relative ratings (1-5 dots, depending on relative potency, but not in a tiered model). When you get one, it manifests in a specific way determined by your Seeming. You can purchase other manifestations from other Seemings if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:32:23-07:00","id":505747,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us a little more about the new Pledge system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T10:53:23-07:00","id":505771,"title":"","content":"Idea for an Arcadian weapon - Blade's Katana. if you don't have permission to wield it, hidden blades pop out of the grip and slice your fingers off! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T16:37:02-07:00","id":506218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=505747#post505747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell us a little more about the new Pledge system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. I'll do that sooner than later. <br /> <br /> Er. I can tell you Matt McFarland wrote it. And he was very passionate about doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T16:47:58-07:00","id":506227,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a name you could have attached to pledges that would have gotten a bigger grin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:07:30-07:00","id":506233,"title":"","content":"Hey, asking here because why not? I'm making a character for a game that will port over into 2e when it comes out and I was curious: is healing people through dreams / Oneirophysics able to be supported in some form in 2e? It's a dream doctor-focused concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:25:34-07:00","id":506254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline?p=506227#post506227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a name you could have attached to pledges that would have gotten a bigger grin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was really glad he made time to work on this book. He did my pledges and fetches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:46:37-07:00","id":512486,"title":"","content":"I have high hopes for that first appendix, the one about mortals who come in contact with the fae. My players first instinct when dealing with anyone unconnected with the freehold is to avoid them (not unreasonable) which makes interacting with mortals difficult. Some ideas about how to introduce someone who has weird dreams (for example) would be excellent. Also hoping for some &quot;cunning folk&quot;/witch types that deal enough with the fae that they know how to protect themselves and maybe have some kind of magic all their own (witch's brews? Taking goblin fruits and mixing them in a pot to create magical potions? Something like that.). How do Lost detect when the fae and the Fae are targetting mortals, and what kinds of strange Wyrd-bound souls do the Lost encounter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}